{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f97e4812067ad7fe","type":"group","x":-5200,"y":-640,"width":5240,"height":2280,"label":"Ideas for Project"},
		{"id":"4748eae2579c1f8b","type":"group","x":-5160,"y":-580,"width":5160,"height":1060},
		{"id":"64033db7cc4c6c98","type":"group","x":-5160,"y":540,"width":5160,"height":1060},
		{
			"id":"02f33af3bdebfe02",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Transparency",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-2200,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"97cd93d8bb4cbe39",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n\n|Dimension|Academic Focus|Industrial Focus|\n|---|---|---|\n|Data Scale|Small, static datasets (e.g., MovieLens)|Massive, dynamic streaming data|\n|Metrics|Precision, Recall, NDCG|Revenue, Conversion, Retention|\n|Latency|Usually not a primary concern|Millisecond-level response requirements|\n|Model Complexity|High (e.g., large LLM fine-tuning)|Optimized (e.g., multi-stage distilled models)|\n|Experimentation|Offline evaluation|Online A/B testing|\n\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2080,
			"y":920,
			"width":560,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"a057add2d775baee",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Online Metrics",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1840,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"7739036ee26ce5a6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Most academic (need to verify) focused on offline metrics like NDCG or hit rate on static datasets. Industries have to operate on severe constraints of scale, latency, and cost.\n\nIndustries would like to focus more on revenue, conversation and retention",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1840,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"e5050be279520787",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Lack of historical data -> poor cold start performance.\nSolved using LLMs with their world knowledge embedded in them.\nEg: a gen model can recomm a movie based on a director's thematic style and current cultural trends without needing an explicit knowledge graph",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2920,
			"y":980,
			"width":320,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"6b61ac852bca72a4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"| Data Strategy                  | Mechanism                                                | Primary Benefit                                      |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| Knowledge-Infused Augmentation | Injecting LLM world knowledge into sparse datasets       | Mitigates cold-start and improves semantic richness  |\n| Agent-Based Simulation         | Using LLMs to simulate diverse user interaction paths    | Enhances model robustness and provides training data |\n| Multi-Domain Unification       | Aligning cross-domain items via semantic representations | Bridges domain gaps and representation misalignment  |\n| Modality-Specific Encoding     | Hierarchical attention for text, images, and audio       | Enables nuanced multimodal user modeling             |\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2920,
			"y":1240,
			"width":760,
			"height":322
		},
		{
			"id":"4177113081d4256f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1480,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2d040c667665720d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Real time modelling and temporal dynamic, latency in milliseconds, idk, read again (ask llm to explain)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1480,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":110
		},
		{
			"id":"3ba54b24689a8e14",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Long term vs short term satisfaction\n\nFocus on long term using RL to model sequential decision making process:: rewards on user loyalty, and lifetime value instead of immediate hit rates",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"26c8aeee874ca6ca",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f0c75447bfe5a845",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Debiasing: Manipulative vs Genuinely Helpful",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-3640,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"218b628cc2f6a7a0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"An empathetic-sounding response can still be manipulative.\n\n> I know you’re feeling lonely… maybe treat yourself with this premium subscription.\n\nIt _sounds_ caring.  \nBut causally it may exploit vulnerability.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3640,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"d3e66ad17f78ae60",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Sequential Recommendation",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-3280,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"954e07cc6512d06d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Gen-AI Shift",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-2920,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9ed8cbe9b364fc2a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"This shift is best understood using three dimensions: data, models and tasks",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2920,
			"y":840,
			"width":320,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"6fc235e9e4cb6b54",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Explainability",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-2560,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fac2f6482680a913",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Presenting recommendations as a sequence, first this, then this then that.\n(All are not presented at once, but based on how many already recommended so far)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3280,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":145
		},
		{
			"id":"96103e1eccd4d4fb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The shift from \"scoring and ranking\" to a generative concept. Synthesis of recommendations, identifies, or even the content itself.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2920,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"230feb97d4f7845d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Causal Inference + Do-Calculus",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4720,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"530e5840858c7146",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Most ML does:\n\nCorrelation learning.\n\nExample:  \nPeople who watch X also buy Y.\n\nCausal reasoning asks:\n\nIf I _force_ someone to see X,  \nwill it cause Y?\n\nThat’s different.\n\nDo-calculus (from Judea Pearl’s framework) formalizes:\n\nInterventions vs observations.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4720,
			"y":686,
			"width":320,
			"height":434
		},
		{
			"id":"392e84495c0401b3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Casual inference\n\nAim, ensure recomm is truly personalized\nHow, casual debiasing fws to eliminate confounding factors like item popularity and demographic variables",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4720,
			"y":1140,
			"width":320,
			"height":211
		},
		{
			"id":"17e87f780d55072f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Metacognitive Controller",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4360,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"eca5367b035c20b1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Metacognition = thinking about thinking.\n\nThe project proposes:\n\nA symbolic module that monitors the LLM.\n\nIt checks:\n\n- Is the LLM hallucinating?\n    \n- Is it contradicting known facts?\n    \n- Is this recommendation aligned with health goals?\n    \n- Is it encouraging over-consumption?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4360,
			"y":686,
			"width":320,
			"height":396
		},
		{
			"id":"ec509b64cc6ef211",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Neuro-Symbolic AI",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-5080,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c729d9ebc9ab6ac1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Neural networks → pattern recognition  \nSymbolic logic → rules + reasoning",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5080,
			"y":686,
			"width":320,
			"height":94
		},
		{
			"id":"5191657aabfcfddc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Neural models (like LLMs):\n\n- Great at language\n    \n- Great at detecting emotion\n    \n- Bad at consistency and logical guarantees\n    \n\nSymbolic systems:\n\n- Explicit rules\n    \n- Logical constraints\n    \n- Knowledge graphs\n    \n- Policy enforcement",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5080,
			"y":820,
			"width":320,
			"height":339
		},
		{
			"id":"d59ff7772284bfdd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Knowledge Graph of Human Values + Legal Policies",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4000,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"3aa152e8222a8357",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Build a structured graph encoding:\n\n- Health guidelines\n    \n- Financial well-being principles\n    \n- Legal regulations\n    \n- Ethical constraints\n    \n\nExample nodes:\n\n- \"Overconsumption\"\n    \n- \"Addiction risk\"\n    \n- \"User long-term goals\"\n    \n- \"Mental health preservation\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4000,
			"y":720,
			"width":320,
			"height":342
		},
		{
			"id":"b48311a4a1799a22",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Not applicable, basically respond accordingly to user's emotion state. \nWe are not generating text anyways. \n\nUh... Does items inherently convey some message, nevertheless we can't know the user's emotion without his language text which are would not process anyways\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-760,
			"y":680,
			"width":320,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"2e826bec46491da1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Emotionally Aware Systems",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-760,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"81de52ba504286f8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Privacy, security and decentralisation",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-400,
			"y":560,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"3ceecf64e08e7582",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Right now, most AI recommenders are:\n\n- Pattern recognizers\n    \n- Engagement optimizers\n    \n- Statistical machines\n\nBut they don’t reason about:\n\n- Is this actually good for you?\n    \n- Is this manipulative?\n    \n- Does this align with your long-term health?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-440,
			"y":-100,
			"width":320,
			"height":414
		},
		{
			"id":"8ce6dfb8bab95d05",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Most current solutions are similar to system 1, intuitive but erroneous (hallucination and lack of deeper logical grounding over the high dimensionality of user preferences) \n\nWe need to move on to system 2, rationality\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1880,
			"y":220,
			"width":320,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"5c02f661e99e14e0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Huh? Maybe i was being too critic of age. It goes much deeper, it might group people based on harmful mentality",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4400,
			"y":100,
			"width":320,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"27c19d7569fd06fd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Fairness",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4400,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"51f962e8a147c9a2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The model can learn sensitive attributes like gender implicitly due to the nature of its algorithm; thus developing a bias.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4400,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":134
		},
		{
			"id":"685ffc53894e36b9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# HCRS\n\nHuman centred recommender systems\n\nPrioritise human values like trust, safety, fairness and well being\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4400,
			"y":-117,
			"width":320,
			"height":197
		},
		{
			"id":"6246fe7caf05b2fb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Federated Learning",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4040,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"7d33cbb1a6ad2ba9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Server sends model → everyone trains locally → they send back gradients → server averages them",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-4040,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":154
		},
		{
			"id":"37e9a849fc127976",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Instead of images or sequences, you train on a **graph**:\nUsers <-> Products  \nUsers <-> Users  \nItems <-> Items",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3680,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":154
		},
		{
			"id":"c21d5baeefadb726",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Client A has set: {A, B, C}  \nClient B has set: {B, C, D}\n\nThey want to know:\n\n> What do we both have in common?\n\nBut without revealing:\n\n- A’s full set\n    \n- B’s full set",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2960,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":334
		},
		{
			"id":"56c92bbfeb0f84db",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"This is about adding **noise** to gradients.\n\nYou may remember:  \nRegularization prevents overfitting.\n\nPrivacy noise prevents:\n\n- Reconstruction attacks\n    \n- Gradient inversion attacks\n    \n\nGradient inversion =  \nSomeone reconstructs your training data from gradients.\n\nAnd multimodal gradients are _much richer_ than simple tabular data.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2600,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":434
		},
		{
			"id":"fff5116c71b5540b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"How do we expand local graphs to improve learning —  \nwithout revealing the full global graph?\n\nThat’s the “sub-graph expansion” problem.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3520,
			"y":-100,
			"width":360,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"e40bcd130e00a4cb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Each user only sees their local graph slice.\n\nBut maybe some neighbors overlap with others.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-3320,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":154
		},
		{
			"id":"1bc63545bf7f7589",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# LLM-Based Persona Agents",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-2240,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"3aab02dbf8cdd7b3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Now imagine each LLM is given:\n\n- A personality\n    \n- Preferences\n    \n- Interests\n    \n- Emotional tendencies\n    \n\nExample persona:\n\n- Loves indie films\n    \n- Gets bored quickly\n    \n- Hates repetition\n    \n- Impulsive late at night\n    \n\nEach of these is an “agent.”\n\nAnd thousands of them interact with recommendation systems.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2240,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":454
		},
		{
			"id":"0b506e39e8f6b826",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# System 1 vs System 2 Recommendation",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1880,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"1d664054c3fb320b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Long Trajectory",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1520,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{"id":"9d471d22c7417d88","type":"text","text":"Trajectory = sequence of interactions over time.\n\nInstead of:\n\nOne recommendation → one click\n\nWe simulate:\n\nDay 1 → 20 recommendations  \nDay 2 → boredom level changes  \nDay 10 → fatigue accumulates  \nDay 50 → agent churns or thrives\n\nSo we model behavior over _months_ of simulated time.","x":-1520,"y":-294,"width":320,"height":394},
		{
			"id":"016a6272e67a3645",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Graph Neural Networks",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-3680,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0fa8eef41e19352c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Sub-graph Expansion",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-3320,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d5e37aa8887a37b4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Local Differential Privacy",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-2600,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"6e03e7dc38e710c7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"This is borrowed from psychology (Daniel Kahneman).\n\n- System 1 = Fast, impulsive, reactive\n    \n- System 2 = Slow, reflective, long-term thinking\n    \n\nIn recommender terms:\n\n**System 1 recommender:**\n\n- Maximizes immediate clicks\n    \n- Shows what grabs attention\n    \n- Optimizes short-term engagement\n    \n\n**System 2 recommender:**\n\n- Optimizes long-term satisfaction\n    \n- Balances novelty and familiarity\n    \n- Avoids burnout",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1880,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":494
		},
		{
			"id":"ab242dd5a49af5c7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Private Set Interaction",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-2960,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"58dcb23c29db2ff1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Modeling Fatigue and Boredom",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-1160,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"110ab0f23574bee4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Model it mathematically like:\nSatisfaction(t) = f(diversity, novelty, repetition, time)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1160,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":174
		},
		{
			"id":"fabae7156c019f36",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Social Welfare Recommender",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-800,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"ceaa31516658203c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Empathetic AI systems",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-440,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9132f60c76501e20",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"to verify whether their recommendations causally improve users’ long-term wellbeing or inadvertently cause harm or manipulation",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-440,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":157
		},
		{
			"id":"01708a8fd5d6f55c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Behavior Aware",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-5120,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"652a6d014e07b607",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Noise Modelling",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4940,
			"y":-540,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"13bc1b51bd7b56ac",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Addiction Aware",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-4760,
			"y":-420,
			"width":320,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b663a9bfa8b2fa28",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### System-1 (Impulsive / Moreishness)\n\nThis is:\n- Instant gratification\n- Dopamine-driven\n- Habitual scrolling\n- Clickbait\n\nProperties:\n- Strong short-term effect\n- Decays quickly\n- Creates a temporary spike in return probability\n\nExample:\nYou binge 10 reels tonight.  \nTomorrow morning you feel the urge to open the app again.  \nBut that urge fades quickly.\n\n\n## System-2 (Utility / Long-term value)\n\nThis is:\n- Meaningful content\n- Learning something useful\n- Getting value aligned with goals\n\nProperties:\n- Smaller short-term spike\n- Longer-lasting effect\n- Drives sustained retention\n\nExample:\nYou watch a high-quality ML lecture series.  \nYou return next week to continue learning.\n\n# A user might keep returning even if the platform only shows moreish content.\n\nBecause if System-1 spikes are large enough and frequent enough, they can sustain repeated returns — even if utility is low.\n\nThis models:\n- Doomscrolling\n- Habit loops\n- Short-term addictive usage\n\nThey are **not** modeling cases like:\n- Clinical addiction\n- Compulsive behavior independent of content quality\n- Structural habit loops that persist even without gratification\n\nTheir model still assumes:\n> Return probability depends on past experience.",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":null
			},
			"x":-4760,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":354
		},
		{
			"id":"a80bed6a6fdbf99c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Normally:\n\nEach user is optimized individually.\n\nHere:\n\nThey optimize for:\n\nTotal well-being across all users.\n\nIt’s like:\n\nIndividual fitness vs public health.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-800,
			"y":-294,
			"width":320,
			"height":314
		}
	],
